  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This Nature news article has begun to circulate beyond its publication venue, with one documented downstream reuse in Europe PMC and one recorded podcast mention. The broader attention record is still thin, but the article is already present in scholarly and community-facing discovery channels.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Max Kozlov\u2019s 2026 Nature article reports on an institutional and legal development at the intersection of COVID-19, public administration, and scientific governance. The record shows immediate visibility in scholarly infrastructure, including indexing in Europe PMC and one documented reuse event, indicating that the piece has already been surfaced in at least one downstream biomedical context.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Evidence of wider uptake is limited but not absent. A single podcast mention in TWiV suggests the article reached an audience engaged with virology and infectious-disease reporting. Beyond that, the public-discourse archive is unavailable, so the record should be read as incomplete rather than silent.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Citation-based impact is still at an early stage: OpenAlex currently records no citations, and scite likewise shows no citing, supporting, or contradicting references. That means there is not yet a scholarly citation trail to summarize, even though the article has already been indexed and reused in at least one biomedical source.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Teaching-adoption evidence is also limited to a WorldCat holdings signal, which indicates library discovery rather than demonstrated classroom use. Overall, the article\u2019s footprint is small but real, with its strongest signals coming from scholarly indexing and a single downstream mention rather than from citations or broad public attention.</p>",
